  {
    "title": "API, data and the design",
    "body": "**API:** each API server calls `allow(key)` before handling a request; refused requests get 429 and `Retry-After` with the seconds until the next token. **Data model:** per key in a shared in-memory store, tokens left and the last refill time, with an expiry a few minutes after the key's last request. **High-level design:** clients → load balancer → API servers, which all check the same **limit store**, with a replica.",
